# The derivation must follow the claim graph.  The artifact chains
# sumcheck -> evalopen and also carries an independent evalopen whose consumed
# claim is an artifact source.  One entry-bodied binding, two occurrences: at
# the chained occurrence the consumed claim is produced by the sumcheck and an
# entry rule selects no premise for it, so the application refuses and names
# the claim; at the independent occurrence the same rule derives, because a
# premise about an artifact source stays the artifact's own hypothesis.
#
# Before this judgment the chained application succeeded and emitted a witness
# pricing one reduction's rounds, with empty premises and empty obligations,
# with nothing in the witness saying the sumcheck contributed a term.

# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: zkc-seal %S/Inputs/chained-open.mlir %zkc-seal-full -o %t/sealed.artifacts > /dev/null
# RUN: %python %S/../SemanticClosure/lib/artifact_handoff.py stage %t/sealed.artifacts %t/sealed.mlirbc

